findings.recommendation:
For Task 8, prefer the non-mutating half — it fixes the blank-header case (the one that actually breaks the '' sentinel) and cannot mangle any legitimate name, because it never removes a character:

```ts
// A title with no visible character at all is the same as no title: fall back to the default name.
// U+200C ZWNJ / U+200D ZWJ appear in this class only as 'not visible on their own' — a real emoji
// sequence always carries visible code points too, so 👨\u200D👩\u200D👧 passes untouched.
const NO_VISIBLE_CHAR = /^[\s\u200B-\u200F\u202A-\u202E\u2066-\u2069\uFEFF]*$/;
if (NO_VISIBLE_CHAR.test(capped)) return '';
```

If the bidi-spoof half is also wanted, strip this class and note that ZWNJ/ZWJ are deliberately absent from it:

```ts
// eslint-disable-next-line no-control-regex
const TITLE_STRIP = /[\u0000-\u001F\u007F-\u009F\u200B\u200E\u200F\u202A-\u202E\u2028\u2029\u2066-\u2069\uFEFF]/g;
```

Whichever is chosen must land in `updateBoard` and in `sanitizeGroupTitle` in the same commit, in the same order relative to trim and cap — see the separate finding on Decision 7 symmetry.

Extract the normalization once and call it from both sites, so the pair cannot drift again:

```ts
// src/data/migration.ts
export function sanitizeGroupTitle(value: unknown): string {
  if (typeof value !== 'string') return '';
  return value.trim().slice(0, GROUP_TITLE_MAX_LENGTH).replace(/[\uD800-\uDBFF]$/, '');
}
```

and have Task 8's `updateBoard` call `sanitizeGroupTitle(incoming)` rather than re-implementing trim+cap. Note that Task 8 currently says the opposite — 'Do not duplicate that sanitizer' (task-08.md:263) reads as 'do not re-run it', which combined with Decision 10's hand-written trim+cap produces two implementations of one rule. Reusing the exported function is both less code and the only way Decision 7 stays true. If reuse is rejected, at minimum add the same `.replace(...)` to `updateBoard` and record the reason in the decisions log.

Either widen the comment to say plainly which fields are still shared and why that is acceptable, or build a genuinely fresh object — one line, no new concepts, and it removes the aliasing class entirely:

```ts
function freshDefaultData(): PluginData {
  return {
    version: DEFAULT_DATA.version,
    settings: { ...DEFAULT_SETTINGS },
    boards: [createDefaultBoard('My Project')],
    tasks: {},
  };
}
```

Caveat before applying: `createDefaultBoard` calls `crypto.randomUUID()`, so the board id would no longer equal `DEFAULT_DATA.boards[0].id`. I checked tests/unit/migration.test.ts — the four DEFAULT_DATA assertions are all about groupOrder identity and value, none compares board ids, so the existing suite is unaffected. Out of scope for this task either way; the comment fix is the zero-risk half.
